# The cross-implementation fixture is written by `tools/gen-agreement.mjs` with
# LF endings and compared byte-for-byte by `tools/ci.ps1`. With core.autocrlf on
# — the Windows default — checkout would rewrite it as CRLF, the generator would
# write LF, and the drift check would fail on every fresh clone for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the renderers.
crates/pl-draw/tests/agreement.json -text

# The font-licence texts are embedded with `include_bytes!`, and both their byte
# length and sha256 are asserted by `the_vendored_faces_are_the_files_notice_records`
# and disclosed in NOTICE for a recipient to verify. With core.autocrlf on — the
# Windows default — checkout rewrites them as CRLF, so every length and hash is
# wrong on Windows for a reason that has nothing to do with the fonts. Pin them to
# LF like the fixture above.
bins/pl-gui/fonts/*.txt -text

# The same rule for the second font directory, which arrived on 2026-08-03 with
# the PNG raster back end. `crates/pl-draw/fonts/Liberation-OFL.txt` is asserted
# exactly the same way — 4,414 bytes and a sha256, by `pl-draw/src/font/tests.rs`
# against NOTICE — and the line above does not cover it. Without this, a Windows
# checkout turns it into 4,516 bytes and breaks the provenance test on a fresh
# clone. The `.ttf` files need no rule: Git treats them as binary already.
crates/pl-draw/fonts/*.txt -text

# The window icon, added 2026-08-05: 16,384 bytes of raw RGBA8 that
# `bins/pl-gui/src/main.rs` `include_bytes!`s and hands to
# `ViewportBuilder::with_icon`, with its length and sha256 asserted by
# `the_window_icon_and_the_ico_are_one_generation`. Git's own heuristic already
# calls it binary — the first pixels of a transparent-cornered icon are NUL — and
# that is exactly why it is pinned here anyway: the file's classification would
# otherwise depend on what the drawing happens to start with, and a redrawn icon
# with an inked top-left corner could quietly become "text" and be CRLF-mangled
# into a hash nobody can reproduce. The `.svg` is genuinely text and takes no
# rule; the `.ico` is binary by content for the same heuristic reason and is
# covered here for the same reason.
bins/pl-gui/icon/polylinker.ico -text
bins/pl-gui/icon/*.rgba -text

# Rust sources are read by tests that `include_str!` their own file and match
# on newline literals, so a CRLF checkout changes what those tests see. The
# first CI run this repository completed failed on exactly that: one test on
# windows-latest, 509 others passing, invisible to every local gate step
# because only a checkout applies the conversion. Pinned to LF everywhere so
# the working tree and the object store agree on all three platforms.
*.rs text eol=lf

# The Ed25519 verification vectors, added 2026-08-05 with the updater's
# signature checking. `crates/pl-core/src/ed25519.rs` include_str!s this and
# runs all 150 Project Wycheproof cases, and its header records the sha256 of
# the upstream JSON it was converted from.
#
# Rust's `str::lines()` strips a trailing `\r`, so a CRLF checkout does NOT
# break the parser -- this is not a bug fix, and pretending otherwise would be
# the kind of comment this project keeps having to correct. It is pinned
# because a security fixture should be the same bytes on every machine that
# checks it, so the recorded hash refers to something reproducible and a future
# change to the parser cannot be broken by a line ending.
crates/pl-core/vectors/*.tsv -text
